    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d24-a1">

                <pb facs="d24-3" n="3" xml:id="pgd24-3"/>


                <head>IA–ECOSOC Position</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><date>undated</date></dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#italic">Under Secretaries Committee Proposals
                        Adopted without Dissent</hi></p>
                <table>
                    <row>
                        <cell>Proposal Number in Under Secretary’s <hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Memorandum (Tab A)</hi></cell>
                        <cell/>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell>4</cell>
                        <cell>That you approve the elimination of nuisance duties on items totalling
                            $18 million as listed in the Under Secretary’s memo at Tab A, with the
                            proviso that additional recommendations be prepared for your
                            consideration in the light of Latin American suggestions to be submitted
                            next month</cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell>6</cell>
                        <cell>We would announce that the Administration will ask Congress for
                            authority to increase from one quart to one gallon the duty free liquor
                            allowance for returning residents of the U.S. for certain specific
                            beverages not similar to beverages produced in the U.S.</cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell>8</cell>
                        <cell>We would apply the new regional untying policy to AID loans signed
                            before November 1, 1969, in cases where the borrower specifically
                            requests such exception and where the procurement process has not yet
                            been initiated.</cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell>10</cell>
                        <cell>At Caracas, we plan to: (a) review recent US actions designed to
                            promote integration including the Presidential commitment to participate
                            in financing construction of the Darien Gap Highway, the decision to
                            permit region-wide procurement with AID funds, and our increased support
                            for export promotion activities; and (b) reiterate our outstanding
                            offers for financial assistance to the Andean Group, CARIFTA and CACM,
                            for which funds are already earmarked in the FY-70 or FY–71 budgets, and
                            to an eventual Latin American Common Market when the necessary
                            preliminary steps have been taken.</cell>
                    </row>
                    <pb facs="d24-4" n="4" xml:id="pgd24-4"/>
                    <row>
                        <cell>11</cell>
                        <cell>We will propose that to encourage greater participation of other
                            donors in Latin America, the merits of various alternatives be discussed
                            at the forthcoming IDB Board of Governor’s meeting in April.</cell>
                    </row>
                </table>
            </div>
